TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"partial","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"A geostationary orbit at 600 km is incorrect. GEO is at about 35,786 km and cannot keep a satellite fixed over a reef at about 18°S latitude. The orbit concept needs to be a LEO or other suitable orbit with revisit and coverage analysis."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"The Gantt chart ends in week 10 (16/11), but the stated final report deadline is 20/11. The schedule should align with the deadline."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"The plan mentions calculating COEs and AOEs but no orbital elements or launch/orbit calculations are shown, so course material on launch and orbits (R2) is not applied in the preliminary work."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The claim of 100 m per pixel bathymetry resolution and the reef-monitoring satellite requirements are not translated into quantified mission requirements (resolution, revisit time, latency)."}],"overall":"The report has a clear, well-referenced reef-monitoring rationale and a readable Gantt chart, but the orbit choice is technically invalid (GEO at 600 km), and preliminary technical results are absent. Scores are given on each level's stated 0–10 scale. Fixing the orbit and adding quantified results would substantially improve the mark.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Rationale and users (marine scientists, conservation, reef-dependent communities) are clear and referenced with footnotes. However, mission requirements are not quantified, and the orbit choice is technically wrong: GEO is about 35,786 km, not 600 km, and it would not hold a fixed position over the reef at about 18°S. This undermines the concept's coherence.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km, which keeps the satellite fixed above the reef at all times."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":15.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A Gantt chart with task descriptions and dates is provided and the plan looks feasible. It lacks explicit contingency or variation provisions and a clear list of information sources. The chart ends in week 10 (16/11) while the stated due date is 20/11, and the link to the mission narrative is only partial.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"The final report is due on 20/11/20 at 5pm."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Only minor progress is evident: tutorials, reading and background research. No technical results, calculations, orbit parameters, or STK outputs are presented, so the work cannot be shown to be on track.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":14.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report has clear headings, consistent footnote citations with matching URLs, and a readable layout. Some awkward phrasing and a minor grammar slip appear, and the Gantt chart lacks a figure caption. Overall, presentation is professional and easy to follow.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Coral reefs harbour some of the most diverse species of life on the planet, but this is not even the full extent of their nurture."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue. Deadlines are indicated by red lines."}]}]}
